  "full_text": "And the signal is given, the guns start to boom out, and there it flies on the masthead, the flag of the new dominion of India. India and Pakistan celebrated their country's freedom from British rule. The euphoria didn't last. When the borders were drawn, people who'd lived alongside each other for centuries now found themselves as a religious minority in a new country. Millions were on the move. This is a horror story. Unpleasant to listen to and even more unpleasant to relate. Some of the worst of the fighting was in Punjab. Its fertile plains became killing fields. All sides were aggressors. All sides victims. This afternoon we saw exactly what a disturbed town looks like. A town...",
